From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2025 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] runner: plain LSCall, so the runner can register with SAM

Since 0010 the runner registers its service by appId, which makes
ls-hubd resolve the *application* role rather than the qml-runner
executable role. That role is "regular", so the connection is not
privileged, and LSCallFromApplication - which asks luna-service2 to
speak for an application and is privileged-only - started failing:

  LSCallFromApplication with application ID org.webosports.app.phone
  but not privileged
  Failed to LSCallFromApplication: -1031

That hit the very first subscribe, registerServerStatus, so the runner
never reached its registerApp subscription and no QML app was ever a
registered app as far as SAM was concerned. SAM answers a relaunch of an
unregistered non-web app by killing it and starting it again, so opening
the app menu - which relaunches the app with "palm-command":
"open-app-menu" - restarted the app instead, and did so for every QML
app on the system.

The appId argument is redundant now: the handle is already an
application service registered for that appId, so the hub attaches the
caller identity by itself and SAM matches the caller by its LS2 name.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific, depends on patch 0010]

Signed-off-by: Herrie <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff --git a/tools/runner/lunaservicewrapper.cpp b/tools/runner/lunaservicewrapper.cpp
index 6db21be..9a32a5a 100644
--- a/tools/runner/lunaservicewrapper.cpp
+++ b/tools/runner/lunaservicewrapper.cpp
@@ -117,17 +117,26 @@ void LunaServiceWrapper::subscribe()
 
     LSError lsError;
     LSErrorInit(&lsError);
-    if (LSCallFromApplication(lunaHandle,
-                              ("luna://" + m_serviceId + "/" + m_method).toLatin1(),
-                              param.toLatin1(),
-                              m_appId.toLatin1(),
-                              (LSFilterFunc) staticCallbackFunc,
-                              this,
-                              &m_token,
-                              &lsError)) {
+    // Plain LSCall, not LSCallFromApplication: the handle is already an
+    // application service registered for this appId, so the hub knows who is
+    // calling and attaches the identity itself. Passing the appId a second
+    // time asks luna-service2 to speak *for* an application, which only a
+    // privileged connection may do - and since the runner started registering
+    // by appId the hub resolves the app's own role, which is "regular". Every
+    // subscribe then failed with -1031, registerServerStatus included, so the
+    // runner never got as far as subscribing to registerApp. SAM saw an
+    // unregistered app and answered a relaunch by killing and restarting it
+    // instead of delivering the event: opening the app menu restarted the app.
+    if (LSCall(lunaHandle,
+               ("luna://" + m_serviceId + "/" + m_method).toLatin1(),
+               param.toLatin1(),
+               (LSFilterFunc) staticCallbackFunc,
+               this,
+               &m_token,
+               &lsError)) {
         m_isSubscribed = true;
     } else {
-        qWarning() << "Failed to LSCallFromApplication:"
+        qWarning() << "Failed to LSCall:"
                    << lsError.error_code << lsError.message;
     }
 }
